  "id": "differential-reinforcement-of-low-rate",
  "term": "differential reinforcement of low rate",
  "definition": "Differential reinforcement of low rate is an operant learning procedure in which reward is available only when responses are kept infrequent, typically by waiting a fixed amount of time before responding. Responding too often lowers performance because it reduces access to reinforcement.",
