      "reasons": [
        "The packet supports that DRL performance depends on withholding a response for a fixed interval and that responding too often reduces access to food reward, but it does not explicitly state that “reward is available only when responses are kept infrequent.”",
        "The definition’s wording that the procedure “typically” involves waiting a fixed amount before responding is only partially supported by the packet’s description of withholding for a fixed interval; the “typically” qualifier and the “reward only when …” formulation are not directly evidenced."
